Modifications: 2 MiB per-PNG limit, 12 MiB aggregate bound, explicit container
Chromium sandbox option, scratch-only test artifacts, reference regression test.

The Go strict verdict decoder is adapted from the same repository's
backend/internal/service/scheduled_test_visual_quality.go under LGPL-3.0.
The reference HTML in this repository is a new implementation, not a copy of
that repository's reference.

Runtime isolation uses canonical HTML allowlisting, disabled page JavaScript,
CSP sandbox/script-src none, offline browser context, blocked network routes,
no external images/fonts, and a supervised 30-second process deadline.
Native Chromium sandbox is enabled by default. Docker explicitly disables it
because ordinary container seccomp/user-namespace settings cannot launch a
sandboxed browser; containers still run rendering as a non-root user with all
of the content restrictions above. This is not an OS-level network namespace.
